WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.840
FedRAMP evidence and documentation are the record of how a cloud service is scoped,

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.660
secured, assessed, operated, and monitored.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.600
They are not the security program by themselves,

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.980
but they make the security program visible.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.880
A reviewer cannot evaluate a control implementation, boundary,

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.940
shared responsibility model,

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.520
or continuous monitoring process if the provider cannot explain what exists and support

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.660
that explanation with evidence.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:32.440
A useful distinction is the difference between a claim, a control implementation,

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.100
and supporting evidence.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.160
A claim says something is true.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.420
A control implementation explains how the system makes it true.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.760
Evidence supports whether the statement is true for the actual system.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.420
For example, saying that privileged access is reviewed is a claim.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:49.840
Explaining the review process is implementation detail.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:54.620
Showing completed reviews, owners, dates, and outcomes is evidence.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.400
Documentation must describe the real system rather than an idealized version of the

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:00.500
system.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:05.600
If diagrams omit dependencies, if narratives describe tools that are no longer used,

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:10.940
or if procedures do not match how teams actually work, the documentation becomes a risk.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:16.200
Stale or generic documentation can mislead assessors, customers, engineers,

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.420
and authorizing stakeholders.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.840
Accurate documentation is part of operational trust.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:27.260
Strong evidence supports assessment, authorization support, continuous monitoring,

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.360
customer reuse, and risk decisions.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:35.620
It helps stakeholders see what is implemented, how it operates, where weaknesses remain,

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.000
and whether remediation is progressing.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.700
The goal is not documentation volume.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.640
The goal is trustworthy information that connects security claims to actual implementation

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.700
and ongoing operation.
